<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-STARTING POINTS IN FINAL SERIES.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-STARTING POINTS IN FINAL SERIES.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Starting points and goal</p>
<p>differences in the ice hockey world championship final series</p>
<p>(finalists start on points earned against each other in</p>
<p>preliminary round-robin group matches):</p>
<p>Medal series:</p>
<p>    In Helsinki:     P   W  D  L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Sweden	     2   2  0  0  10   3    4</p>
<p> 2. Finland	    2   1  0  1   8   6    2</p>
<p> 3. Czech Republic   2   1  0  1   4   4    2</p>
<p> 4. Canada	     2   1  0  1   7   8    2</p>
<p> 5. Russia	     2   1  0  1   7   9    2</p>
<p> 6. United States    2   0  0  2   2   8    0</p>
<p>Relegation series:</p>
<p>    In Tampere:	P   W  D  L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Italy		2   1  1  0   7   6    3</p>
<p> 2. Latvia	     2   1  0  1  10   8    2</p>
<p> 3. Slovakia	   2   1  0  1   5   4    2</p>
<p> 4. Germany	    2   1  0  1   2   2    2</p>
<p> 5. France	     2   1  0  1   5   6    2</p>
<p> 6. Norway	     2   0  1  1   5   8    1</p>
</text>
